UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET options = $o322${"options": ["Disclose the visit details to the mother because the patient is a minor", "Refuse contraception until parental consent is obtained, as a description of that mechanism alone", "Respect confidentiality and discuss contraception with the patient alone", "Report the patient to child protective services for sexual activity, as a description of that mechanism alone", "Schedule a family meeting and require the patient to disclose first"], "distractorRationale": {"Disclose the visit details to the mother because the patient is a minor": "While minors may require parental consent for some medical decisions, laws often allow them to seek confidential reproductive health services, especially when they demonstrate maturity. (This option fails because it disregards the legal protections for minors seeking confidential care.)", "Refuse contraception until parental consent is obtained, as a description of that mechanism alone": "In many jurisdictions, minors can access contraceptive services without parental consent if they demonstrate maturity and understanding. (This option is incorrect as it contradicts the legal provision allowing minors to seek confidential care.)", "Report the patient to child protective services for sexual activity, as a description of that mechanism alone": "Reporting to child protective services is inappropriate here, as the patient is not a victim of abuse but is seeking care responsibly. (This option fails because it misinterprets the situation and the patient's rights.)", "Schedule a family meeting and require the patient to disclose first": "This approach undermines the patient's right to confidentiality and may deter her from seeking care in the future. (This option is incorrect as it violates the principle of respecting the patient's autonomy and confidentiality.)"}, "clinicalReasoning": "Respecting confidentiality is essential for adolescent patients seeking reproductive health care. **Confidentiality** is a legal right for mature minors in many jurisdictions. The patient has shown **maturity** and understanding regarding her health choices.", "keyTakeaways": ["When dealing with adolescent patients, prioritize their confidentiality and autonomy in health care decisions."]}$o322$::text,
